  "differences": "Original explicitly mandates 'very long, elaborate' length and 'realistic comic scene' tone; A omits 'realistic comic' tone specification and simplifies length to 'extensive'; B changes tone to 'funny, realistic' (adding 'funny'), simplifies length to 'super long', and adds 'backstories' which were not explicitly requested as a separate element from character description. Original specifies 'one woman or more'; A and B imply plurality ('female characters', 'group of women') but lose the specific 'one or more' logical constraint. Original lists specific challenge types (dare/bet/contest/challenge); A generalizes to 'challenge', B generalizes to 'dare'. Original demands 'meticulous detail' for the act and reactions twice; A retains 'meticulous', B uses 'really descriptive' and 'focus on'. Original strictly constrains scene to 'only female characters'; A says 'feature female characters' (ambiguous if males can be present as non-participants), B says 'group of women' (implies focus but less strict exclusion of background males)."
